{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","title":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":356,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","line":851,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Ricci curvature lower bound]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound}\n\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature}\n\n  Let $n=\\dim M$.  Say that $(M,g)$ has\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}\\ge(n-1)k\\,g$ if, for every $p\\in M$ and $v\\in T_pM$,\n  \\[\n    (n-1)k\\,g(v,v)\\le \\operatorname{Ric}(v,v).\n  \\]\n  In particular, for a unit vector $v$ this reads\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}(v,v)\\ge(n-1)k$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Ricci curvature lower bound] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368362d72696363692d6c6f7765722d626f756e64\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-ricci-curvature\">↗ def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n=\\dim M$\">$n=\\dim M$</span>. Say that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> has <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}\\ge (n-1)k\\, g$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}\\ge (n-1)k\\, g$</span> if, for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_pM$\">$v\\in T_pM$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  (n-1)k\\, g(v,v)\\le \\operatorname {Ric}(v,v).  \\]\">\\[  (n-1)k\\, g(v,v)\\le \\operatorname {Ric}(v,v).  \\]</span> In particular, for a unit vector <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> this reads <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Ric}(v,v)\\ge (n-1)k$\">$\\operatorname {Ric}(v,v)\\ge (n-1)k$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-sec-bounds","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#lem:pet-ch6-bonnet-synge-index-core","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","title":"def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature","label":"def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric","title":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric","label":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-geometric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter","title":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter","label":"thm:pet-ch6-myers-ricci-diameter"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","title":"def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Ricci curvature lower bound]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch6-ricci-lower-bound}\n\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-ricci-curvature}\n\n  Let $n=\\dim M$.  Say that $(M,g)$ has\n  $\\operatorname{Ric}\\ge(n-1)k\\,g$ if, for every $p\\in M$ and $v\\in T_pM$,\n  \\[\n    (n-1)k\\,g(v,v)\\le \\